full_original_path_pool.summaryOfChange:
- Capture that the gNB-CU determines the QoS for PC5 Relay RLC channels over each PC5 hop for multi-hop relay;
- Add multi-hop relay related terminologies;
- Capture the Peer UE information for PC5 Relay RLC channel.

Added signalings for inter-CU LTE with NR-DC:
- extend S-NG-RAN node Addition Preparation procedure;
- extend M-NG-RAN node initiated S-NG-RAN node Modification Preparation procedure;
- extend S-NG-RAN node initiated S-NG-RAN node Change
- extend XN-U Address Indication

Add multi-hop relay related terminologies;
Capture that single-hop relay protocol stack can be applicable to the multi-hop relay case with additional Intermediate Relay UE(s);
Capture that the signalling flow for path switch from direct to single-hop indirect path can be also applicable to path switch from direct path to multi-hop indirect path with additional U2N Relay UE(s);
Add the Remote UE’s initial access procedure via Multi-hop relay.

Added signalings for:
- Extend the existing Handover Preparation procedure;
- Introduce a new LTM Configuration Update procedure;
- Introduce a new Cell Switch Notification procedure;
- Introduce a new LTM Cancel procedure;
- Introduce a new TA Information Transfer procedure;
- Introduce a new CSI-RS Coordination procedure.

Following functions were added and modified:
A new procedure was added to enable indicating handover success;
Handover Preparation procedure was enhaced to enable indicating conditional HO and parallel transactions are allowed (and the requested target cell ID is added to identify responses to the possible parallel requests);
Handover Preparation procedure was enhaced to enable replacing prepared CHO;
A new procedure was added to enable CHO cancellation from the target side; 
CHO cancellation from the target and from the source may be done per target cell.
SN Status transfer procedure may be used for DAPS HO.
A new procedure was added to facilitate early data forwarding.
Indication of the max no of acceptable CHO requests for given UE and the probability for CHO execution was added to the CHO HO preparation.
Support for the early data forwarding was added also for MR-DC configuration.

Impact assessment towards the previous version of the specification (same release): 
The CR has functional impact on selected procedures, as listed below, because it adds new functionalities and enhances some others.
